From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Austin Schuh <austin.linux@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Feb 2025 01:11:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] uvcvideo: Cap USB bandwidth to 1/N of reported on compressed
 video

The UVC_QUIRK_FIX_BANDWIDTH quirk in uvc_fixup_video_ctrl only fires when
the format is NOT compressed (the test begins with
!(format->flags & UVC_FMT_FLAG_COMPRESSED)). MJPEG-compressed cameras
(e.g. Arducam IMX477 in MJPEG mode) report a dwMaxPayloadTransferSize that
exceeds the USB endpoint's actual bandwidth, causing isochronous transfer
overruns and frame drops. The native code skips the bandwidth-reduction
logic for compressed formats entirely.

Add an else-branch that applies a runtime-configurable divisor to the
camera's reported dwMaxPayloadTransferSize when the quirk is set and the
format is compressed. Default divisor of 1 is a no-op; set
bandwidth_quirk_divisor=8 (or similar) at module-load time to cap
compressed-format bandwidth.

This is a device hack; the proper fix would be to teach the UVC stack to
compute compressed-format bandwidth correctly, but that requires per-codec
knowledge the UVC class spec doesn't expose.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [device hack]
Signed-off-by: Austin Schuh <austin.linux@gmail.com>

Ported from the 5.15 (linux-jammy-nvidia-tegra) version to 6.8
(linux-noble-nvidia-tegra): the non-compressed branch was refactored (now
computes a bandwidth estimate and clamps to >=1024) and the header include
list was reshuffled, but the modification point - the
dwMaxPayloadTransferSize assignment at the end of the non-compressed
branch - is unchanged in intent.

---
 drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c b/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c
index bfa3c69..cccf2ec 100644
--- a/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c
@@ -21,6 +21,9 @@
 #include <linux/atomic.h>
 #include <asm/unaligned.h>
 
+static int bandwidth_quirk_divisor = 1;
+module_param(bandwidth_quirk_divisor, int, 0660);
+
 #include <media/jpeg.h>
 #include <media/v4l2-common.h>
 
@@ -258,6 +261,16 @@ static void uvc_fixup_video_ctrl(struct uvc_streaming *stream,
 		bandwidth = max_t(u32, bandwidth, 1024);
 
 		ctrl->dwMaxPayloadTransferSize = bandwidth;
+	} else if ((format->flags & UVC_FMT_FLAG_COMPRESSED) &&
+			(stream->dev->quirks & UVC_QUIRK_FIX_BANDWIDTH) &&
+			stream->intf->num_altsetting > 1) {
+		uint32_t prior = ctrl->dwMaxPayloadTransferSize;
+
+		if (bandwidth_quirk_divisor > 1)
+			ctrl->dwMaxPayloadTransferSize /= bandwidth_quirk_divisor;
+		uvc_dbg(stream->dev, VIDEO,
+			"Reducing compressed bandwidth from %u B/frame to %u B/frame\n",
+			prior, ctrl->dwMaxPayloadTransferSize);
 	}
 
 	if (stream->intf->num_altsetting > 1 &&
